      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Analysis and presentation",
      "text": "Analysis organises evidence to answer the question; presentation makes the relevant pattern visible. Maps, graphs, tables, isolines and flow charts serve different purposes. Choose according to variable type, spatial or temporal structure and the intended comparison. A chart chosen for appearance alone can mislead if it uses inappropriate units, categories or a hidden denominator.",
      "claim_ids": [
