      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A data table should have a title, clear headings, units, site or time labels and a source where relevant. Retain raw readings or identify summaries. Missing values need an explicit code. Rows and columns should not silently change meaning. A table of widths in centimetres and depths in centimetres can contain both, but their headings must prevent them being combined as if they measured the same feature.",
      "claim_ids": [
