    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Totals, means, percentages and ranges answer different questions. A mean uses the valid total divided by the number of readings; a range is highest minus lowest; a percentage needs the stated denominator. Consider widths 10,20,30 centimetres: mean twenty, range twenty, but the equal numbers are coincidental measures of different features. A record should show the calculation and unit before interpreting it geographically.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.07-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.07-2",
