    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A bar chart compares separate categories using a labelled value axis and consistent bar treatment. A line graph is useful for a suitable ordered sequence, such as observations through time, where joining the points has meaning. Joining unrelated named categories with a line can imply continuity that the data do not possess. Choose the display for the actual relationship rather than because both forms can be drawn by software.",
      "claim_ids": [
