    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A pie chart displays parts of a whole. The categories must share a denominator and be exhaustive without inappropriate overlap. A quarter corresponds to ninety degrees and half to 180 degrees. Counts of ten, twenty and ten out of forty correspond to 25%,50%,25% and angles 90°,180°,90°. If responses allow several choices per person, the totals may not form a single non-overlapping whole suitable for an ordinary pie.",
