    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A dispersion display shows individual values and their spread rather than just a mean. Two samples can have the same mean but different variation. For example, 10,20,30 and 18,20,22 both average twenty, with ranges twenty and four. Displaying the values helps prevent the mean from being mistaken for every observation. Repeats and spread can inform reliability without requiring advanced statistical tests.\n\n![Two samples with the same mean of 20 but ranges of 20 and 4](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-4.1-034-INTERP-answer.png)",
      "claim_ids": [
