      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A map locates evidence spatially. A choropleth shades defined areas by classes of suitable rates or ratios. Raw counts across unequal areas can mislead if the intended comparison is density. Include a non-overlapping key, date and units. A regional average does not describe every point inside the boundary, so the map's scale and aggregation should remain part of interpretation.",
