    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A teaching example gives A twenty people per square kilometre and B ten, with classes zero to less than ten, ten to less than twenty and twenty or more. A enters the highest class and B the middle. Both boundaries are unambiguous. Darker shading should consistently represent the intended direction; it must not be reversed halfway through or assumed to mean better conditions without reading the key.",
