    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Isolines connect points of equal value in a continuous field, such as elevation, rainfall or another suitable measured quantity. Label the interval and use observations to estimate positions between known points where appropriate. Do not connect every station regardless of value. Isolines should represent the field logically; two different value lines should not cross in a simple single-valued surface.",
