    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "If station A has value ten and B twenty along a straight segment, a value-fifteen line would cross halfway under a stated linear-interpolation assumption. That is an estimate between observations, not a new measurement. Sparse data or a non-linear field limits precision. The display should retain source points or make their support clear enough to understand where interpolation was needed.",
