      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A flow chart shows a sequence, decision or causal structure through boxes and directional arrows. An enquiry chart might connect question, method, data, analysis, conclusion and evaluation, with a revision loop. A process chart should distinguish direction and any branching. It is different from a map flow line showing movement quantities; the key and context identify what the arrows mean.",
