      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Display design should preserve comparability. Use consistent units, scales and category definitions across panels intended for comparison. A truncated value axis can exaggerate a bar difference if not clear; unequal observation periods can distort totals. Label sources and uncertainty where relevant. The goal is an interpretable geographic comparison rather than the most dramatic-looking image.",
