      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An appropriate presentation can reveal a limitation as well as a result. Missing points, wide spread or unmatched periods should remain visible. Removing them without a documented reason can make the figure look stronger than the evidence. Keep the underlying data and calculation trail so another reader can reconcile the display with the record and the hypothesis.",
