    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A coast dataset can connect distance to sediment. At stations zero,fifty and 100 metres along a safe route, longest-dimension readings are 10/12/14, 20/22/24 and 30/32/34 millimetres. The means are twelve, twenty-two and thirty-two millimetres. A scatter or suitable ordered-distance plot can display the increasing relationship. Raw samples remain useful because each mean summarises three values rather than a single pebble representing the station.",
