    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A separate gradient record at those stations uses falls of forty,fifty and twenty-five centimetres over ten horizontal metres. Convert the run to 1,000 centimetres before comparing: the ratios are 1:25,1:20 and 1:40. The middle station is steepest and the last flattest, so gradient does not steepen at every step along the route. Grain-size and gradient hypotheses can therefore have different conclusions from the same set of stations.",
