      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Presentation should retain a declared sign. For tracer movement, north-positive displacements +3,+2,−1,+4 metres can be shown on a signed number axis or suitable chart. A plot using only absolute distances would hide the southward exception. The missing fifth tracer should have a missing-value note rather than a zero bar. The visual then supports both the net movement and its limits.",
