      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A comparison of group percentages can use bars with the same zero-based percentage axis. Resident positives twelve of twenty and visitor positives sixteen of twenty produce bars at 60% and 80%. An axis ending below 100% can be used only with clear labelling and an appropriate purpose, while a truncated baseline can exaggerate the difference. The point difference is twenty percentage points, not twenty people.",
