    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.07-20",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "An environmental scale must carry direction into every display. Suppose a pollution score runs from zero least to five most pollution. A managed site changes from four to two while a reference changes from three to four. The first improves under the score and the reference worsens. Label the scale and sites so a lower bar is not mistaken for a lower quality outcome.\n\n![Pollution scores before and after at a managed and a reference site (0 = least pollution)](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-4.1-046-INTERP-answer.png)",
