      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Units also constrain chart choice. A bar representing a count should not share an unlabeled scale with a percentage or a distance. Separate panels or clearly explained axes can compare related variables without pretending they are the same quantity. Labels should name the quantity, period and unit, while the written interpretation explains the relationship rather than treating a visual crossing as a measured geographic event.",
